#: views/changelog.php:1600
msgid "BuddyPress xProfile Groups and Fields"
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1604
msgid ""
"The theme uses the BuddyPress xProfile groups and fields to allow site "
"members to enter information about themselves, like bio, personal, "
"interests, social links and account information."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1608
msgid ""
"To be able to show each xProfile field group and its respective fields in "
"different settings pages and widgets in the members profiles, the theme has "
"to query them by their name."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1612
msgid ""
"This creates problems if users need to edit group or field names for "
"translations purposes, as the theme won't be able to find and display the "
"group or field information if the name is not the one it is expecting."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1616
msgid ""
"To solve this and allow users to translate them, we have included a new "
"customizer section with this update (\"Vikinger Settings\" -> \"xProfile "
"Groups / Fields\")."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1620
msgid ""
"To understand how to edit the profile groups and fields for translation "
"purposes, we need to detail how the theme uses the group names."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1624
msgid ""
"xProfile group names consist of a prefix part (i.e. \"Profile\") followed by "
"an underscore (_) followed by the subgroup name (\"Bio\"): \"Profile_Bio\"."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1628
msgid ""
"The prefix part (in this example \"Profile\") is used to identify on which "
"settings page the group and all its fields will be displayed in, to allow "
"members to edit their information:"
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1636 views/troubleshooting.php:277
msgid ""
"\"Profile\" prefix: groups and fields display on the member profile info "
"settings screen (Profile_Bio, Profile_Personal, Profile_Interests)."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1644 views/troubleshooting.php:285
msgid ""
"\"Social\" prefix: groups and fields display on the member social settings "
"screen (Social_Links)."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1652 views/troubleshooting.php:293
msgid ""
"\"Account\" prefix: groups and fields display on the member account info "
"settings screen (Account_Info)."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1660
msgid ""
"The prefix part of the xProfile group names shouldn't be changed, otherwise "
"the sub groups and fields won't display correctly in the settings pages."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1664
msgid ""
"The subgroup name part (in this example \"Bio\") is used to identify on "
"which member profile page widget the subgroup fields are going to be "
"displayed in (in this case, the \"About Me\" widget)."
msgstr ""

#: views/changelog.php:1668
